A core charges its turn for the ticks it counts but does not note them,
so it charges the same ticks again as its next trap counts up to the machine's count;
a core counts the machine's ticks once each.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: thread's account is stamped ahead of the count

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -477,7 +477,6 @@ static void tick_advance(uint32_t ticks)
             turn->stamp += owed;
         }
         core->turn_from = 0;
-        core->ticks += owed;
     }
     sched_ticks += ticks;
     uint32_t nearest = sched_ticks + NEAREST_NONE;
